// Restart the target so a serial capture sees the boot from t = 0.
// This is the "run it again and watch" probe of tools/trace_read.py: start the
// capture first, then run this, and the records of bring-up and of the first
// (full screen) refresh land on the wire instead of before the terminal is
// attached. See docs/charter.md §11.
//
// Because the reset goes through the debugger's reset line and the panel's
// RESX is tied to NRST, the panel gets a proper pulse here rather than the
// slow supply ramp of a cold power-on - the one case it needs seconds to
// recover from.
//
//   r   reset, stopping at the reset vector
//   g   run it
//   qc  close; the target is left running
//
// No flash write, no memory change. Connection parameters stay on the command
// line, one fact in one place (see tools/flash.sh).

r
g
qc
